WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.700
From deep sea sci-fi to a Hitchcock classic, if&nbsp;
you want to see any of these movies or TV shows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.136
you'd best dig out the DVD player — because&nbsp;
you won't find them online anytime soon.

00:00:10.136 --> 00:00:13.320
Despite being one of the most successful&nbsp;
directors in the history of cinema,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.880
some of James Cameron's back catalog remains&nbsp;
unavailable online. Take, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.800
the 1994 Arnold Schwarzenegger film True&nbsp;
Lies, which cannot be rented, purchased,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.678
or streamed legally in the United States…&nbsp;
although it is available on Disney+ in the UK.

00:00:27.678 --> 00:00:32.820
Another such film is The Abyss, a 1989 sci-fi&nbsp;
film about a group of scientists who attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.440
to recover a sunken nuclear submarine and its&nbsp;
crew. As they explore the depths of the ocean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.618
the team comes across a non-terrestrial&nbsp;
intelligence surrounding the damaged craft.

00:00:41.618 --> 00:00:46.560
The Abyss wasn't exactly a huge success at&nbsp;
the box office, grossing just over $50 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:52.038
domestically, but it won plenty of plaudits from&nbsp;
critics and has since become a minor cult classic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.038 --> 00:00:56.460
However, while it was previously streaming on&nbsp;
Netflix, The Abyss has not been available to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.480
watch on the internet for an extended period&nbsp;
of time. In fact, the movie hasn't even been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.916
released on Blu-ray — although Cameron himself has&nbsp;
hinted that a 4K remastered release is on the way.

00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:09.840
Based on the Thomas M. Disch story of the&nbsp;
same name, The Brave Little Toaster is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:15.060
1987 animated film from director Jerry Rees. It&nbsp;
follows an anthropomorphic toaster who comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.900
life when humans aren't around, kind of like&nbsp;
a more breakfast-y version of the toys from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.220
Toy Story. Along with a wide array of other&nbsp;
electrical appliances, the toaster sets out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.337
to try and find its owner after they fail to&nbsp;
return to the holiday home for several years.

00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:29.578
"Things could be worse, you know."

00:01:31.379 --> 00:01:34.499
"How? How could they be worse?"

00:01:34.499 --> 00:01:35.760
"They couldn't, I lied."

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.380
Despite limited success at the box office,&nbsp;
The Brave Little Toaster was able to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.940
some popularity on home video and received&nbsp;
largely positive reviews from critics. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:48.420
film was broadcast on the Disney Channel&nbsp;
and enjoyed a small theatrical release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:53.520
and was later followed by two sequels: The Brave&nbsp;
Little Toaster to the Rescue and The Brave Little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.900
Toaster Goes to Mars, both of which are available&nbsp;
to stream online through Disney+. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:03.336
the original film is absent from any streaming&nbsp;
service and cannot be purchased or rented online.

00:02:03.336 --> 00:02:08.400
Although many modern TV fans might not know it,&nbsp;
Murphy Brown was one of the most popular sitcoms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:14.040
on television through the 1980s and 1990s. It&nbsp;
aired for nearly a decade and broadcast a total&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:19.980
of 260 episodes across that time. Candice Bergen&nbsp;
portrayed Murphy Brown, a recovering alcoholic who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.420
works as an investigative journalist. And if you&nbsp;
need proof that Murphy Brown was a bona fide pop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.280
culture phenomenon, take a look at the countless&nbsp;
awards it won, including numerous Primetime Emmys.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.020
So why is Murphy Brown destined to remain&nbsp;
solely in the world of physical media? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.520
it's complicated. For one thing, the show was&nbsp;
produced by Warner Bros. despite airing on CBS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.500
so it's not actually clear where it could stream.&nbsp;
It also utilized a large amount of music, meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.760
the songs would all need to be licensed all&nbsp;
over again — and the sheer number of Motown hits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.500
featured in the series makes it cost-prohibitive.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, you won't have much luck finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.997
this show on modern home media, either, as&nbsp;
only the first season was ever released on DVD.

00:02:56.997 --> 00:03:01.140
Moonlighting was a comedy-drama series&nbsp;
that starred Bruce Willis as a private&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:07.200
detective and Cybill Shepherd as his business&nbsp;
partner. Airing on ABC between 1985 and 1989,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.500
the series crossed genres,&nbsp;
frequently broke the fourth wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.820
and included a number of fantasy elements.&nbsp;
The show was also responsible for bringing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:19.140
Willis to the public's attention and had a&nbsp;
hit theme song from jazz star Al Jarreau.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:24.240
Moonlighting garnered a positive reception and won&nbsp;
a number of high-profile awards, including several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.040
Primetime Emmys. However, it has failed to appear&nbsp;
online in any form, with some outlets suggesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.600
that this may be due to music rights issues. The&nbsp;
series contains a large number of songs in every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:39.692
episode and licensing all of that music might not&nbsp;
be worth the cost of adding it to Hulu or Disney+.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.500
"Kids today — it's always gimme, gimme, gimme."

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:49.140
Let It Be is a 1970 documentary film that&nbsp;
charts the creation of The Beatles' final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:53.640
studio album. The film features no narration&nbsp;
or interviews, instead showing the musicians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.300
as they prepare for the upcoming record&nbsp;
by rehearsing songs and discussing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:01.260
recording process. Although there are no&nbsp;
obvious fights depicted in the documentary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.820
the tension between each of the band's members&nbsp;
is palpable; Let It Be provides a fascinating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:09.780
glimpse into the internal conflicts that would&nbsp;
cause them to split up a month before the movie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.796
release. The film culminates in a full recording&nbsp;
of the band's iconic final rooftop concert.

00:04:14.796 --> 00:04:18.120
While Let It Be has been given a few&nbsp;
limited home media releases in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.560
it has not been reissued or made available&nbsp;
via streaming. Speaking to Rolling Stone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.660
Paul McCartney refuted rumors that he had blocked&nbsp;
its release, but even today fans still cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:32.580
access the original documentary. However, much of&nbsp;
the footage from the film was later used in Peter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:37.676
Jackson's documentary series The Beatles:&nbsp;
Get Back, which is available on Disney+.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:42.780
Kevin Smith's View Askewniverse movies might not&nbsp;
be to everyone's tastes, but films like Clerks and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:48.780
Chasing Amy have accrued dedicated fan followings&nbsp;
and widespread praise from critics. The 1999 film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:52.680
Dogma is in the same mold, although it hasn't&nbsp;
enjoyed the same attention as some of Smith's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.480
other releases. Featuring an ensemble cast driven&nbsp;
by a whole heap of star power, the story follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.680
a group of religious figures attempting&nbsp;
to prevent two fallen angels from defying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.617
God's will by returning to heaven — an act that&nbsp;
would have disastrous consequences for reality.

00:05:06.617 --> 00:05:09.660
The main issue blocking Dogma from&nbsp;
streaming online appears to stem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.540
from a disagreement between Smith&nbsp;
and Harvey Weinstein. The director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.560
told Cinema Blend that Weinstein owns the&nbsp;
rights to the film and that the disgraced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.616
producer is blocking a sale that would&nbsp;
give Smith control over its release.

00:05:20.616 --> 00:05:25.320
The Fall is a 2006 movie by Indian&nbsp;
director Tarsem Singh. Based on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:29.760
Bulgarian film Yo Ho Ho, the story follows&nbsp;
a stuntman who befriends a young girl in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:34.020
hospital while recovering from a number of&nbsp;
severe injuries. To help stave off boredom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:38.100
he tells his companion fantastical stories&nbsp;
that come to life in the girl's imagination.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:43.380
Starring Lee Pace as the stuntman Roy Walker,&nbsp;
the film received mixed reviews and didn't fare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:47.820
particularly well at the box office — although&nbsp;
Roger Ebert gave it four out of four stars and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:52.920
recommended it as a once-in-a-lifetime experience.&nbsp;
Produced without any major studio involvement, The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:57.480
Fall has failed to materialize on any streaming&nbsp;
platforms and isn't available to rent or buy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:02.956
meaning the only way to see it is by tracking&nbsp;
down one of the limited DVD or Blu-ray releases.

00:06:02.956 --> 00:06:07.080
Before he found widespread fame in Brooklyn&nbsp;
Nine-Nine, Andre Braugher was one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:10.860
stars of another police-based television&nbsp;
series: Homicide: Life on the Street.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:15.564
"Do you know what gravitas&nbsp;
sounds like? Greetings. All."

00:06:15.564 --> 00:06:20.280
Based on the David Simon book that would&nbsp;
also inspire The Wire, this NBC series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:26.880
ran from 1993 until 1999, spanning seven&nbsp;
seasons, 122 episodes, and a TV movie.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:32.340
The show is highly regarded by many; in 2007,&nbsp;
Time even counted it among the best television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:36.420
shows ever made. Life on the Street was&nbsp;
also nominated for dozens of awards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:40.980
including a number of Primetime Emmy Awards.&nbsp;
Several different DVD releases have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.420
released over the years, but there is currently&nbsp;
no way to legally access it online. This may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.320
well be another music rights issue, as the&nbsp;
show features a lot of contemporary music,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:53.700
although the involvement of a number of different&nbsp;
production companies probably didn't help, either.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:58.560
Directed by Scott Hicks, the 1996&nbsp;
movie Shine is largely based on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.160
real-life events surrounding pianist&nbsp;
David Helfgott. From a young age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.880
the future musician is forced to learn to&nbsp;
play at the insistence of his abusive father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:10.860
but the pressure of performing eventually leads&nbsp;
him into a mental health crisis. Geoffrey Rush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:15.240
brought the tortured pianist to life in Shine&nbsp;
and won considerable acclaim for his performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.320
while the film in general was almost&nbsp;
universally praised by critics and audiences.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:24.240
Sadly, Shine is not available for streaming&nbsp;
in any location. The movie was released on DVD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.040
shortly after its theatrical debut, while&nbsp;
a Blu-ray version came out in 2010 — so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.197
while it's not easy to find and&nbsp;
watch, it's not impossible either.

00:07:32.197 --> 00:07:37.680
Green Street Hooligans is a 2005 crime film&nbsp;
that stars Charlie Hunnam and Leo Gregory as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:42.120
British football hooligans who are joined by an&nbsp;
American visiting his family. The film charts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.560
how the Green Street Elite fights other rival&nbsp;
groups and travels to football matches across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:50.640
the country. However, events quickly take&nbsp;
a tragic turn as Elijah Wood's character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.278
Matt, is exposed to the gruesome&nbsp;
consequences of hooligan culture.

00:07:54.278 --> 00:07:58.200
Those living outside of the US might have more&nbsp;
luck being able to watch Green Street Hooligans:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.560
It's available to buy and rent on&nbsp;
a variety of services in the UK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:04.440
for example, including Microsoft, YouTube, Amazon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:09.660
and Apple. This may well be because Green Street&nbsp;
Hooligans, known simply as Green Street in the UK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:15.060
simply lacks international appeal, as the subject&nbsp;
matter is very specific to that country. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:19.657
it has not been picked up by any overseas&nbsp;
streaming services or digital distributors.

00:08:19.657 --> 00:08:23.880
Based on the comic series of the same name,&nbsp;
Tales from the Crypt was an HBO anthology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:29.880
series that ran for seven seasons between&nbsp;
1989 and 1996. It mixed elements of horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:34.260
comedy, and dark fantasy to deliver stories&nbsp;
that often included graphic violence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:38.520
mature themes. The series was hosted by a&nbsp;
mysterious figure known as the Cryptkeeper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:42.660
who would introduce storylines and talk directly&nbsp;
to the viewer. Over the years, a number of guest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:47.400
stars featured in Tales from the Crypt, and&nbsp;
the series also received a number of spin-offs.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.560
"What's the matter with you? Want to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:53.700
that 90lb corpse for the rest&nbsp;
of your death? Keep pumping!"

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:58.440
The show's absence from modern streaming&nbsp;
services — including HBO Max — appears to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:02.760
be due to complicated rights issues. TNT&nbsp;
executive Kevin Reilly even told Deadline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:07.200
that Tales from the Crypt suffers from the most&nbsp;
complicated rights structure has ever seen in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:11.340
his career." The fact that the comic book series&nbsp;
has been sold multiple times to different owners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:16.696
has undoubtedly made it even harder to reboot&nbsp;
or re-release the franchise in recent times.

00:09:16.696 --> 00:09:20.160
Created by Jon Beckerman and Rob Burnett&nbsp;
with the help of David Letterman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.640
Ed is a comedy-drama series that&nbsp;
first hit television screens in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:27.720
2000. The show follows Tom Cavanagh's&nbsp;
character Ed Stevens, a down-on-his-luck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.980
lawyer who loses his job after making an&nbsp;
expensive mistake. To make matters worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:36.180
he discovers that his wife is having an affair.&nbsp;
Ed immediately decides to go back to his hometown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:40.020
where he chases the affections of a local&nbsp;
woman and reunites with his best friend.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:45.660
Having run for four seasons and received generally&nbsp;
positive reviews, you'd probably expect Ed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:49.920
available on a variety of platforms — but it&nbsp;
isn't. Even the show's creators are unsure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.240
why it hasn't been added to any digital service,&nbsp;
with Burnett suggesting that it might be due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:58.920
a combination of music rights and the fact that&nbsp;
NBC-Universal and Paramount co-own the series.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:06.060
The 1940 Alfred Hitchcock movie Rebecca is a film&nbsp;
adaptation of Daphne du Maurier's 1938 novel of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:10.320
the same name. Rebecca stars Laurence Olivier as&nbsp;
a widower who falls in love with a young woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.680
played by Joan Fontaine. Like many&nbsp;
of Hitchcock's other films, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:17.520
this is not so much a simple romance as&nbsp;
it is a psychological thriller — one that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:21.180
revolves around a dark secret in the&nbsp;
widower's past. The movie was a huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.900
success when it was released and won two&nbsp;
Academy Awards, including Best Picture.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.360
Even with its award success and acclaim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:32.220
Rebecca cannot be watched in any digital format.&nbsp;
It occasionally airs on Turner Classic Movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:36.720
and the Criterion Collection has released&nbsp;
the film on both DVD and Blu-ray. The fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.560
that it is not available digitally has never&nbsp;
been explained, and it's all doubly confusing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:45.636
considering that many other celebrated Alfred&nbsp;
Hitchcock films are readily accessible online.

